# <%= it.projectName %>

<%= it.config.framework === 'nestjs' ? 'NestJS' : it.config.framework %> REST API<% if (it.hasDatabase) { %> backed by <%= it.config.database %> through <%= it.config.orm %><% } %>.

Generated with [scafoldercli](https://www.npmjs.com/package/scafoldercli). This
project is yours: nothing depends on the generator at runtime.

## Requirements

- Node.js <%= it.nodeVersion %> or newer
<% if (it.hasDocker) { -%>
- Docker (optional, for the database and for running the app in a container)
<% } -%>

## Getting started

```bash
cp .env.example .env
<% if (it.hasDocker && it.hasDatabase) { -%>
docker compose up -d <%= it.config.database %>
<% } -%>
<%= it.config.packageManager %> install
<% if (it.isPrisma) { -%>
<%= it.config.packageManager %> run db:migrate
<% } -%>
<%= it.config.packageManager %> run start:dev
```

The API listens on <http://localhost:<%= it.port %>>.

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `start:dev` | Run with hot reload |
| `start:prod` | Run the compiled build |
| `build` | Compile to `dist/` |
| `lint` | Lint and autofix |
| `format` | Format with Prettier |
<% if (it.hasTests) { -%>
| `test` | Run the test suite |
| `test:watch` | Run tests in watch mode |
| `test:cov` | Run tests with coverage |
<% } -%>
<% if (it.isPrisma) { -%>
| `db:migrate` | Create and apply a migration (development) |
| `db:deploy` | Apply pending migrations (production) |
| `db:generate` | Regenerate the Prisma client |
| `db:studio` | Browse the database |
<% } -%>

## Health

| Endpoint | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /health/live` | The process is running. Use for liveness probes. |
| `GET /health/ready` | The process can serve traffic<% if (it.hasDatabase) { %>, including database access<% } %>. Use for readiness probes. |
<% if (it.hasAuth) { -%>

## Authentication

| Endpoint | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /auth/register` | Create an account |
| `POST /auth/login` | Exchange credentials for tokens |
| `POST /auth/refresh` | Rotate a refresh token |
| `POST /auth/logout` | Revoke the current session |
| `POST /auth/logout-all` | Revoke every session for the user |
| `GET /auth/me` | The authenticated user |

Access tokens are short-lived. Refresh tokens are stored hashed, rotated on
every use, and revocable. Reusing a rotated refresh token revokes the entire
session family — the standard response to a suspected token theft.
<% } -%>
<% if (it.hasDocker) { -%>

## Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

The image is multi-stage, runs as a non-root user, and takes all configuration
from the environment. Nothing in the build depends on paths from the machine
that generated it.
<% } -%>

